=== ApiError
kind: term
src: api/src/errors.rs :: pub enum ApiError {
doc: Every way the API refuses a request. Each refusal has a name, sent to the console as error_code, and a status: 400 for a bad request, 401 for not signed in, 403 for not allowed or over quota, 404 for not found, 409 for a conflict, and 503 when no address is free. The console chooses what to tell the person by the name.

=== store_lock
kind: term
src: api/src/db/datastore.rs :: pub fn lock(
doc: The API keeps everything in memory behind one lock. Each piece of work holds the lock from its first check to its last write, so two requests cannot both pass a check and then both write.

=== console_state
kind: term
src: console/console_state.ts :: export const console_state
doc: Everything the console is showing: who is signed in, their projects, the project on screen with its instances and disks, and the message at the top. Actions change it and the screen draws from it.

